{"nodes": [{"id": "src_help_discogs_article", "label": "Discogs help article (src/help/discogs.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "src/help/discogs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_help_discogs_token", "label": "Discogs personal access token", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/help/discogs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The token stays on the computer with GLUE Home and goes only to Discogs. GLUE Home checks it with Discogs and says Connected as. It only reads: nothing is changed on Discogs."}, {"id": "src_help_discogs_in_glue_count", "label": "In GLUE: N songs / Not in GLUE", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/help/discogs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In GLUE: N songs means GLUE has songs of that record: the record's title as their album, by one of its artists (a compilation: on its label). Not in GLUE means none were found, for example a record only on vinyl or with different names here."}, {"id": "src_help_discogs_covers", "label": "Covers from Discogs (help)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/help/discogs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Discogs is often the only source for vinyl and white labels, so it is asked when the other services have none."}, {"id": "src_help_discogs_pace", "label": "Discogs reading: daily, on Refresh, about one request a second", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/help/discogs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GLUE Home reads the lists again once a day and on Refresh. Discogs allows about one request a second, so a big collection takes a minu